.prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/samsung-tv-state-findings.md", ".prawduct/changes/audit-wave-1.md", ".prawduct/runbooks/moving-the-pi-player-to-a-new-revision.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "A bracketed Host with text after the bracket other than ':port' is now refused, and no test pins it", "recommendation": "Instance. It broke because the O-2 fix added a second refusal to `_split_authority` beyond the port check: `if rest and not rest.startswith(\":\"): return \"\", None` (src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py:169). Before it, `Host: [::1]junk` split to name `::1` with no port and was answered 200; now it is refused with a 421. That is changed behaviour at a trust boundary with no test at all: the new parametrizations (`test_a_host_whose_port_is_not_a_port_is_refused_and_not_an_error`, the Origin twin) all use `127.0.0.1:<port>`, and the only bracketed hosts in tests/test_settings_ui.py are the accepted `[::1]:{port}` forms, so deleting lines 169-170 leaves the suite green. Add a bracketed case (for example `[::1]x`, `[::1]80`) to the Host-refused parametrize, asserting 421 and no password set, and one to the Origin twin if that path is meant to refuse it too.", "files": ["src/arrt_player/settings_ui/server.py", "tests/test_settings_ui.py"], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "R-2's construction closed the writes pair; the wall's own pair (`_wall_retry` / `_not_our_wall`) has the same divergence", "recommendation": "R-2 named a class: whether the set is somebody else's is spread over several fields with no single source of truth. `_HeldWrites` now moves the writes' wait and episode together (frame.py `_HeldWrites.held` / `.released`, all four former clear sites call `released`), and the new test pins the named path. Re-running the finding's reason over the remaining fields: `_wall_retry.clear()` runs in `_wall_is_answering` (the set's announcement, a successful show), but `_not_our_wall.end()` runs only in `is_ours` when it reads art (frame.py:348). `is_ours` is consulted only when the wanted work is not the one on the wall, so if the feed changes during a programme so that the wall's current work is wanted again, the set's return to art clears the wait but leaves `rotation.wall_not_ours` open; the next evening's no is then unsaid and `rotation.wall_returned` never appears. Narrower than R-2's path, same shape. Remedy by the same construction (one owner for the wall's wait and episode), with a test: not ours, feed republished to the work on the wall, art again, not ours again, expecting two `rotation.wall_not_ours`. R-2 is left out of resolutions for this reason; the writes half is done.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261119T172527Z-139c337a", "fid": "R-2"}, "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "R-1's standing is a new decision the plan does not record, and the plan's F1 rationale still says the owner is never slowed", "recommendation": "Record gap, rides the commit already owed: write it in .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-audit-wave-1.md under Decisions made mid-build. The fix took R-1's suggested construction (auth.Throttle.vouch / forget_standing, standing for SESSION_SECONDS, not charged to the ceiling; tests cover two guessers filling the ceiling, restart, expiry, password change and setup), and security-model.md describes it. But the plan's DECISION at line 77 still rests on 'the owner's address is never the one being slowed', and no DECISION entry records standing or its residual trade. State that trade as the code has it: a device that has never signed in, or not since the password changed, is held whenever the ceiling is full, and two guessing addresses can keep it full for as long as they keep guessing (each slot that ages out goes to whoever asks first), so 'up to ten minutes at a time' understates it.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261119T172527Z-139c337a", "fid": "R-1"}, "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "R-3's 'said once more when quiet' happens only when a later refusal arrives, and the shared count's window and end are untested", "recommendation": "`RefusedHosts._forget` runs only inside `refused()` (server.py:252, 275), so a name's unsaid count is said when some later refusal arrives, never on its own; if refusals stop altogether the last count is never said. observability-strategy.md's row ('once more when it has been quiet 10 minutes with refusals unsaid') and the class docstring read as if it happens on time. The `_others` window line and its forget line (server.py:280) have no test; the names-cap test sends each name once. Neither changes the bound R-3 asked for (lines per name per window, table size), which is tested. If wanted, make the row relational ('when the next refusal arrives') and add an `_others` case on a commit already happening.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261119T172527Z-139c337a", "fid": "R-3"}, "oid": "O-3"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": "audit-wave-1", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["08", "10"], "chunks_proposed": ["08", "10"], "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/observability-strategy.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/security-model.md"], "chunk_graded": "08", "chunks_graded": ["08", "10"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-audit-wave-1.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "span": null, "bounde